# Updating to a new Project Zomboid build

Run this when PZ ships a new build and you want to target it.

## 0. Confirm the installed build

- Don't trust `%USERPROFILE%\Zomboid\version.txt` — it only rewrites when the game
  **launches**. Check the real install: Steam → PZ → Properties → Betas (branch) and the
  file dates of `...\ProjectZomboid\projectzomboid.jar`, or the Steam
  `appmanifest_108600.acf` (`buildid`, `LastUpdated`, `BetaKey`).
- This is also the `<version>` string you pass to `mise run decompile` below — use the full
  `Major.Minor.Patch` (e.g. `42.20.2`, not `42.20`), since patches can change Java behavior
  too.

## 1. Snapshot the old build BEFORE Steam updates it

Each build's decompile lives in its own `.decompiled/<version>/` folder (gitignored), so
running `mise run decompile` for the new build never touches an older one — but you still
need to have *run it* for the currently-installed build before Steam overwrites it:

```
mise run decompile 42.19.0      # or whatever §0 says is currently installed
```

## 2. Align the type stubs (Umbrella submodule, if used)

```
git -C Umbrella fetch --tags
git -C Umbrella checkout <matching-tag>
git add Umbrella
```

## 3. Re-decompile the new build

```
mise run decompile 42.20.2
```
This also snapshots the installed `media/lua` alongside the decompiled Java in the same
step, so the Java and its Lua callers for this build sit together — this is the authoritative
source for **behavior** (client vs server vs synced), not just signatures.

## 4. Diff the override surface

```
git diff --no-index .decompiled/42.19.0/source .decompiled/42.20.2/source -- <file>
git diff --no-index .decompiled/42.19.0/media/lua .decompiled/42.20.2/media/lua -- <file>
```

TODO: list the specific Java/Lua files this mod's override surface actually touches, mirroring
PlumbingFixed's UPDATING-PZ.md §4 table, so a future update knows exactly what to diff.

Three outcomes per spot:

- **No diff** — nothing to do.
- **Diff** — vanilla behavior changed; reconcile the affected guard/util. Verify authority
  per side in the new `.decompiled/` (golden rule in [CLAUDE.md](../CLAUDE.md)) — never
  adjust a predicate just until it goes green.
- **Seam moved** — a caller left Lua for Java (or vice versa). That's a re-derivation: find
  where the behavior went and what seam replaces it.

## 5. Update the build markers (only if the minimum target changed)

- `Contents/mods/__MOD_NAME__/42/mod.info` → `name=` and `versionMin=`/`versionMax=` if
  applicable.
- `workshop/workshop.vdf` → any `title=... [B42.<x>+]` line.

## 6. Test, clean up, release

- `mise run check`, then a full SP + MP pass per [TESTING.md](TESTING.md).
- Then follow [RELEASING.md](RELEASING.md).
